        "created_at": "2013-06-07T19:29:45.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>For those of you who are familiar with the Extra Credits team on Penny Arcade, James is starting up a fundraiser to talk to the folks in Washington about the good that video games can do in the world.&nbsp; As anyone who plays video games is aware, video games do not automatically transform you into a raving psychopath bent on murdering the whole world, and James wants to take a proactive approach rather than a reactive one whenever another horror story about someone who happened to play video games doing something horrible appears on the news.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>This covers the good games can do for science, awareness of world events, language acquisition, connecting with others, etc.&nbsp; He's not talking about Math Blaster or Number Muncher here.&nbsp; The point is, he can explain it way better than I can here.&nbsp; So, if you're so inclined, click the link and watch his pitch.&nbsp; See if it's worth kicking in five or ten bucks.&nbsp; I know it was worth it for me.<br><br>http://www.rockethub.com/projects/25243#description-tab</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:38:37.753Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
